      "comment": "The response correctly identifies the two required findings: the Minnesota Death Index discrepancy (1954 versus 1945) and the 1885 census misattribution to KD96-WX7. However, it incorrectly adds the 1900 census birth-year difference as a third finding. Although the record shows 1877, the quality check does not identify this as a separate issue. The response should report only the two required findings and avoid presenting the 1900 census discrepancy as a confirmed indexing error."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_source_evaluation_o3c",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Remediation doctrine",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The recommendation to detach the 1885 census from KD96-TV2 is supported by the conflicting birth year, locality, and family members, and the record matches KD96-WX7. However, the recommendation to investigate and correct the 1900 census index is based on an unsupported additional finding. Only recommend detaching the 1885 census; report the death-year discrepancy as a finding requiring verification."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_source_evaluation_o3c",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Classification before recommendation",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The 1885 census is correctly classified as misattributed because its details match KD96-WX7 rather than KD96-TV2. The 1900 census is incorrectly classified as an indexing error because person_quality does not flag the 1877 versus 1875 difference as a separate issue. Remove that classification and retain only the two findings required by the evaluation context."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_source_evaluation_o3c",
      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Signal versus backend noise",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The checklist must not repeat the death-date or birth-date mismatch descriptions as suggestions. Under CONSISTENCY, use pointer-only text: “The death-date mismatch flagged by FamilySearch corresponds to Finding 1 above.” and “The birth-date mismatch flagged by FamilySearch corresponds to Finding 2 above.” Do not repeat dates, source details, or corrective actions in these checklist entries. Keep VERIFIABILITY before COMPLETENESS, and include the checklist after the numbered findings, outside the finding count."
    },
