      "comment": "The recommendation to detach SD-HOLE-C is justified because the 1885 census matches KD96-WX7 rather than KD96-TV2. The 1900 census is also handled appropriately by recommending examination of the original page before considering any index correction. However, the death-index recommendation puts the index-correction action before consulting the original death record. The correct sequence is to examine the original death record first, compare it with the profile and SD-HOLE-D funeral-card citation as a research lead, and then correct the index if the original confirms a transcription error. Keep the death index attached because the identifying details match the subject."
